/E (The circumgalactic medium \(CGM\) is the vast, diffuse gas surrounding galaxies. It plays a critical role in galaxy evolution, star formation, and gas recycling. One of the best tracers of cool gas in the CGM is Mg II absorption, which appears in the spectra of background quasars.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [1]
